ORDER I.—DERMOPTEROUS FISHES.

Sub-Order I.—PHARYNGOBRANCHS.

This order is named from the cutaneous vertical fins, in which the mucoid rays are extremely soft and delicate, or altogether imperceptible, and from the want of pectoral or ventral members. The first two sub-orders are founded on the different developments of the respiratory organs. In the first the pharynx itself is organized for respiration, and two processes having the function of gills project freely into the cavity of the mouth;
